THE REGISTERED VERSION:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	The game was tested on an 020 Amiga 2000 with 4 megs of 32bit ram as
well as on an 030 Amiga 2000 with only 1 meg of 32bit ram and 8 megs of
16bit ram. The 020 won the test for speed hands down even though the 030
was a 25mhz and the 020 was 14mhz. The reason is simply in the 32bit
ram. The more you have the faster this sucker will run. The movement code
was built in such a way that the map only redraws the line the player is
currently moving on or the line that the player moved from. It will also
occassionally redraw the text shown in the window unless there is no
text on the present square or if the present square text is the same as
the last square text.

Below are as many things that I can think of which were added to the
registered version which do not appear in the unregistered version.
However, i am sure as soon as this file hits the archive i will think
of a dozen more!


1> ANIMATIONS - These are not as cheezy as they were in "BATTLE LANDS".
	Just wait till you teleport or astral travel. I like them!

2> The mounts which are supposed to teleport and astral travel can now
	do it. Also there are a couple of more mounts which can travel on
	land and water (amphibious).

3> The astral realms exist. There are are 8 others besides the Earth
	Realm. Of course, they are not as big as the Earth Realm but they
	have the potential to become bigger.

4> All the mundane and special skills work. Some of these are pretty
	impressive as far as what you can do. In fact, one makes it possible
	so that you can move anywhere you want but you'll need a whopping
	501 points in that skill.

5> Unique encounters. Come across a unique encounter and kill them and
	you will never face them again.

6> Teleport squares. You can step onto a teleport square and be thrown
	to another location.

7> Combat will sometimes effect your mount. Hey, these monsters are
	sometimes hungry for a pony as well as for you so they might just
	take	a poke at your mount instead of you.

8> Alignment squares. Bet you wondered why you needed an alignment, eh??
	Well some places you try to go will repell differing alignments and
	some will even cause damage to you.

9> Race squares. Some races have set up special areas where those from
	different races may not pass.

10> Gods of wrath! Sorry, that was a blatant METAL CHURCH plug but this
	is a very good song ("GODS OF WRATH" that is). But now after you die
	you can be brought back to life and given things like money, health,
	jewels and experience all because your god wants you to succeed. This
	will make you think long and hard when you die and it asks if you
	wish to save your game....moohaha!

11> The plot thickens. This is not an actual addition but the plot does
	indeed thicken. You now need to make sure you get certain items in
	some instances to proceed to new areas. It is not always a matter
	of knowing the password.

12> I am going to be adding about 30 new maps on a whole new continent
	in August so the world (which already has 99 maps) will have about
	30 more including some new Impossible Missions and Clergy Quests.
	(BTW That is August 1994. And those who have just seen Battle Lands
	updated in a major way know that I do like to update my games a lot!)


.....Wayne Stewart


